{"type":"ATTR","ticket":31,"id":"ie29"}||{"partId":"","groupId":"","locked":false,"zIndex":29,"parentId":"ie21","key":"Design_Notes","value":"CAP1296-1-AIA-TR; 3.3V supply; fixed 7-bit I2C 0x28. DFN10 exposed ground pad is numbered 11 in this custom symbol and footprint. All six CS inputs wired through 1k resistors to ELE0..ELE5. CS3/SG used as CS3, no guard. R6=10k IRQ pull-up; C11=100nF/C12=1uF supply bypass. Enable only physically fitted electrodes in firmware; disable and ground unused CS inputs per datasheet. Tune thresholds and filtering on actual enclosure. Measure I2C rise time with final bus capacitance and existing pull-ups. GPIO40 IRQ is preserved and is not RTC deep-sleep wake. Firmware critical: clear 0x2A MULT_BLK_EN bit7 for simultaneous grip/rim touches; keep MTP_EN disabled and 0x20 MAX_DUR_EN bit3=0 for long grip. Any unused CS channel must be disabled and grounded, not left floating. Engineering candidate, not tested hardware.","keyVisible":false,"valueVisible":false,"x":0,"y":0,"rotation":0,"color":null,"fillColor":null,"fontFamily":null,"fontSize":3.93701,"strikeout":false,"underline":false,"italic":false,"fontWeight":false,"align":"CENTER_MIDDLE"}|
